# Build context for the API image (docker build . / docker-compose "api" and "scheduler" services).
#
# The context is sent to the Docker daemon and may be copied into image layers, so anything listed here is
# kept out of both. The Dockerfile COPYs only app/, alembic.ini and migrations/; everything below is either
# a secret, personal data, or simply not needed to run the API. The frontend has its own context
# (frontend/.dockerignore). tests/test_docker_context.py checks that this file never removes something the
# Dockerfile needs, and never lets a secret through.

# Version control, CI, editors, assistants
.git
.github
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.remember

# Secrets and local configuration (including .env.example: the image reads its settings from the environment)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Python environments and caches
venv
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Node: the frontend is built from its own context
frontend
**/node_modules

# Database dumps and seed data: real personal data lives in dumps, and the seed has a published admin password
**/*.sql
**/*.dump
**/*.bak

# Generated certificates carry donor names; they are runtime data, never image content
app/static/images/certificates

# Not needed at runtime
tests
docs
scripts
graphify-out
**/*.pdf
*.md
FIX_LOG.md
